From 57e9d0f9c6053c4d988a9a18fc4b646d79b61ac7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:43:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] 7, edge, next: Use mainline tools for microblaze

The microblaze build sets use binutils 2.36 with 13 patches from the
Xilinx meta-xilinx layer, and GCC 12 with 13 Xilinx patches and three
RTEMS patches.  The comment says MicroBlaze GCC and binutils are not
upstream, which is no longer true.

The binutils patches a 32-bit MicroBlaze needs have been upstream since
2023: the TLSTPREL fix (54fd15eef72), the address extension
instructions (b90eb3e5b25), the bit-field instructions and their
masking fix (bb0d05ff74f, 2d1777b530d, 1a5e256f200), the constant range
check (2677a57064a) and the R_MICROBLAZE_32_NONE reloc (d605374748f).
The others are obsolete, Xilinx-local, or concern 64-bit MicroBlaze.
So the build sets use the default binutils.

Of the GCC patches, 0001 to 0007 change only the testsuite.  0010 fixes
a crash with -msmall-divides and -mxl-barrel-shift, a combination no
RTEMS BSP uses by default, and 0011 and 0012 are optimizations.  0008
and 0009 fix the atomic compare and swap, which GCC fixed with
84e2023455a0 (PR target/118280), in 15.3.0 but not in 15.2.0.  0013
removes the broken moddi3.S, which GCC fixed with 3a721dc02388 on master
and 382046ec124a on releases/gcc-15, not in 15.3.0.  The three RTEMS
patches are still needed: the GCC releases lack __USE_INIT_FINI__ (added
on master as 271186ef4643), _init() and _fini() in crti.o, which newlib
calls, and __ELF__, which rtems-libbsd needs.

Add tools/rtems-microblaze-gcc-*-newlib-head.cfg, which include the
default GCC configuration of the build set and add the patches it
lacks, and use them for microblaze.  The rtems-xilinx-* configurations
are then unused.

I built 7/rtems-microblaze on arm64 macOS and ran the sptests and
samples of the petalogix_s3adsp1800 BSP in upstream QEMU: 231 of 235
pass.  One is a regression from the RTEMS 7 tools: samples/cdtest
hangs after its first caught C++ exception.  It passes when linked with
-Wl,--no-relax, so linker relaxation breaks exception unwinding with
binutils 2.47.  next and edge are not built.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
